      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While it's good that you've washed the wound, it's still a good idea to have a doctor check it out. Rusty trowels can harbor bacteria like E. coli or tetanus, which can cause infections if not treated properly. Applying peroxide may help clean the wound, but a doctor can assess the severity of the laceration and provide guidance on wound care and potential antibiotics. It's better to err on the side of caution and get a professional evaluation.",
      "source": "target",
